{"book":16,"chapter":6,"rubric":"FROM ASSEMBLER TO C / ABSTRACTIONS IN C / CHAPTER 6","slides":[{"title":"A function is an address","sub":"Chapter 6 · function pointers","short":"Address","main":"A function pointer is a code address; a call is an indirect jump, jalr.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Function = address","A label in a register","Indirect call"],"captions":["A function is code at some address; a function pointer is a variable holding that address","In assembly you did the same: the label's address was loaded into a register with la","An indirect jump jalr through a register is exactly a call through a function pointer"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"f","x":100.0,"y":70.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"code of function add","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"a","x":100.0,"y":40.0,"text":"0x10450","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"mono":true},{"t":"cell","id":"p","x":270.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":34.0,"text":"fp\n0x10450","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":220.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":166.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"yellow","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":80.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["la   a5, add","li   a0, 2","li   a1, 3"],"hl":[0],"lang":"asm","size":10.5,"lh":18.0,"w":200.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":122.0,"text":"a5 = address of add","size":9.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["int (*fp)(int, int) = add;","int r = fp(2, 3);"],"hl":[1],"lang":"c","size":9.0,"lh":18.0,"w":190.0},{"t":"code","id":"a~code","x":215.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["la   a5, add","jalr a5"],"hl":[1],"lang":"asm","size":10.0,"lh":18.0,"w":140.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":122.0,"text":"call via register, not by label","size":9.5}]],"cues":[14.8,34.0]}]},{"title":"Syntax and typedef","sub":"Read inside out","short":"Syntax","main":"Parentheses around the star are mandatory; typedef gives a short name.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Read inside out","Parentheses required","typedef"],"captions":["int (*op)(int, int): op is a pointer to a function with two ints returning int; read inside out","Without parentheses, int *op(int, int) is a function returning a pointer: the parentheses around the star are mandatory","typedef gives a short name; a function name turns into its address, a call is parentheses after the variable"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["int (*op)(int, int);"],"lang":"c","size":12.0,"lh":20.0,"w":320.0},{"t":"text","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":90.0,"text":"op is a function pointer","size":9.5},{"t":"text","id":"n2","x":180.0,"y":112.0,"text":"(int, int) → int","tone":"green","size":9.5,"mono":true}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["int (*op)(int, int);   // pointer","int  *op(int, int);     // function → int *"],"hl":[0],"bad":[1],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":22.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["typedef int (*binop)(int, int);","binop f = add;     // no & needed","int r = f(2, 3);  // no * needed","binop ops[4];      // array"],"hl":[0],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":19.0,"w":330.0}]],"cues":[14.4,25.3]}]},{"title":"Function table","sub":"Instead of switch","short":"Table","main":"The index is the opcode, the cell is the handler; one indirect jump.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["switch","Table","Where it is used"],"captions":["A long switch over an opcode is a chain of comparisons; every new case grows the branching","An array of pointers: the opcode is the index, the cell holds the handler's address; one indirect jump, time independent of the number of cases","This is how VM interpreters, command dispatchers, and interrupt tables work; the price: the body cannot be inlined"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["switch (op) {","case 0: return add(a, b);","case 1: return sub(a, b);","case 2: return mul(a, b);","}"],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":18.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"t0","x":70.0,"y":36.0,"w":90.0,"h":28.0,"text":"ops[0]","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"t1","x":70.0,"y":72.0,"w":90.0,"h":28.0,"text":"ops[1]","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"t2","x":70.0,"y":108.0,"w":90.0,"h":28.0,"text":"ops[2]","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"f0","x":250.0,"y":36.0,"w":90.0,"h":28.0,"text":"add","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"f1","x":250.0,"y":72.0,"w":90.0,"h":28.0,"text":"sub","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"f2","x":250.0,"y":108.0,"w":90.0,"h":28.0,"text":"mul","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e0","x1":116.0,"y1":36.0,"x2":204.0,"y2":36.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":116.0,"y1":72.0,"x2":204.0,"y2":72.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":116.0,"y1":108.0,"x2":204.0,"y2":108.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":150.0,"text":"ops[op](a, b)","size":10.0,"mono":true}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":60.0,"y":40.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"interpreter","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":40.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"command dispatcher","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c~cell","x":300.0,"y":40.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"interrupts","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n~cell","x":180.0,"y":100.0,"w":280.0,"h":28.0,"text":"downside: compiler can't see the target","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[12.6,24.9]}]},{"title":"Callbacks","sub":"Function + context","short":"Callback","main":"void *ctx next to the function is a manual closure.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Callback","Context","Closure by hand"],"captions":["A callback is a function passed to another function so that it calls it at the right moment: \"how to walk\" is separated from \"what to do\"","A callback has no memory: pass void *ctx alongside it, a counter, a buffer, any data","The pair \"function + context\" is a manual closure; the caller must keep the context alive long enough"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["void each(int *a, int n,","          void (*fn)(int)) {","    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)","        fn(a[i]);","}"],"hl":[3],"lang":"c","size":9.5,"lh":18.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["void each(int *a, int n,","      void (*fn)(int, void *), void *ctx) {","    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)","        fn(a[i], ctx);","}"],"hl":[1,3],"lang":"c","size":9.0,"lh":18.0,"w":350.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"f","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":110.0,"h":30.0,"text":"code: sum_cb","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c~cell","x":90.0,"y":110.0,"w":110.0,"h":30.0,"text":"data: int total","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"p","x":270.0,"y":85.0,"w":100.0,"h":40.0,"text":"pair\n(fn, ctx)","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":146.0,"y1":60.0,"x2":220.0,"y2":76.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":146.0,"y1":110.0,"x2":220.0,"y2":94.0,"tone":"yellow","arrow":true,"width":1.6}]],"cues":[17.4,33.1]}]},{"title":"qsort","sub":"Sorting any data","short":"qsort","main":"Comparison returns a sign; don't subtract, it can overflow.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Signature","Comparison","Subtraction trap"],"captions":["qsort takes the start, the element count, the element size, and a comparison; it knows nothing about the element type","The comparison gets two const void * to elements and returns <0, 0, or >0; inside, cast to the right type","return x - y can overflow and give the wrong sign; write (x > y) - (x < y); qsort is not guaranteed stable"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["qsort(a, n, sizeof a[0], cmp);"],"lang":"c","size":11.0,"lh":20.0,"w":340.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":90.0,"text":"start · count · size · comparison","size":9.5},{"t":"text","id":"m","x":180.0,"y":112.0,"text":"void qsort(void *, size_t, size_t, int (*)(const void *, const void *))","size":7.0,"mono":true}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["int cmp(const void *p, const void *q) {","    int x = *(const int *)p;","    int y = *(const int *)q;","    return (x > y) - (x < y);","}"],"hl":[3],"lang":"c","size":9.0,"lh":18.0,"w":350.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["return x - y;              // ✕","// INT_MIN - 1 → overflow","return (x > y) - (x < y);  // ✓"],"hl":[2],"bad":[0],"lang":"c","size":9.5,"lh":22.0,"w":350.0}]],"cues":[13.7,24.7]}]},{"title":"bsearch","sub":"Search by key","short":"bsearch","main":"Key and element may differ in type.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Sorted array","Key and element","Own key type"],"captions":["bsearch searches a sorted array in O(log n): each step calls the comparison with the key","The comparison gets a pointer to the key and a pointer to an element; the types can differ","This finds a structure by a single field, such as a number, without building a second instance"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":40.0,"y":60.0,"w":44.0,"h":26.0,"text":"2","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":86.0,"y":60.0,"w":44.0,"h":26.0,"text":"5","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":132.0,"y":60.0,"w":44.0,"h":26.0,"text":"8","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a3","x":178.0,"y":60.0,"w":44.0,"h":26.0,"text":"11","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a4","x":224.0,"y":60.0,"w":44.0,"h":26.0,"text":"14","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a5","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":44.0,"h":26.0,"text":"17","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":110.0,"text":"middle → 11 > 8 → go right","size":9.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["int key = 11;","int *r = bsearch(&key, a, n,","                 sizeof a[0], cmp);"],"hl":[1],"lang":"c","size":9.5,"lh":20.0,"w":340.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":118.0,"text":"r == NULL if not found","size":9.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["struct rec { int id; char *name; };","int by_id(const void *k, const void *e) {","    int id = *(const int *)k;","    return id - ((const struct rec *)e)->id;","}"],"hl":[3],"lang":"c","size":8.5,"lh":18.0,"w":350.0}]],"cues":[12.6,29.9]}]},{"title":"Generic container","sub":"Bytes, size, operations","short":"Container","main":"The address of element i is base + i * size; the compiler sees no types.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Three parts","Element size","Operations together"],"captions":["A generic container needs: data as bytes, the element size, and a set of operations on an element","The size tells how far to step and how much memcpy should copy: the address of element i is base + i * size","Comparison and destruction live in a structure; no type safety, consistent sizes are on the author"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":60.0,"y":60.0,"w":100.0,"h":30.0,"text":"void *data","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":60.0,"w":100.0,"h":30.0,"text":"size_t size","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":300.0,"y":60.0,"w":100.0,"h":30.0,"text":"operations","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":118.0,"text":"bytes + size + behavior","size":9.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"m0","x":74.0,"y":60.0,"w":70.0,"h":26.0,"text":"e0","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"m1","x":146.0,"y":60.0,"w":70.0,"h":26.0,"text":"e1","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"m2","x":218.0,"y":60.0,"w":70.0,"h":26.0,"text":"e2","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"m3","x":290.0,"y":60.0,"w":70.0,"h":26.0,"text":"e3","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":110.0,"text":"addr(i) = (char *)data + i * size","size":9.5,"mono":true}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":10.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["struct vtype {","    size_t size;","    int  (*cmp)(const void *, const void *);","    void (*drop)(void *);","};"],"hl":[2,3],"lang":"c","size":9.0,"lh":18.0,"w":350.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":140.0,"text":"the compiler won't notice int instead of char *","tone":"red","size":9.0}]],"cues":[15.6,31.1]}]},{"title":"Operations table","sub":"Interface in C","short":"Interface","main":"An object holds a pointer to a table: polymorphism without language support.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Interface","Object with vptr","Inheritance, C style"],"captions":["A structure of function pointers is an interface: a set of operations that each type implements","Every object stores a pointer to its type's table; generic code calls area() through it, not knowing a circle from a rectangle","A concrete struct starts with a common header: a pointer to it converts to a pointer to the first field, inheritance in the C style"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["struct shape_ops {","    double (*area)(const void *);","    void   (*draw)(const void *);","};"],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":19.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"o1","x":60.0,"y":50.0,"w":80.0,"h":30.0,"text":"circle","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"o2","x":60.0,"y":100.0,"w":80.0,"h":30.0,"text":"rectangle","tone":"blue","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"t1","x":190.0,"y":50.0,"w":90.0,"h":30.0,"text":"circle ops","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"t2","x":190.0,"y":100.0,"w":90.0,"h":30.0,"text":"rect ops","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":100.0,"y1":50.0,"x2":144.0,"y2":50.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":100.0,"y1":100.0,"x2":144.0,"y2":100.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":320.0,"y":76.0,"text":"s->ops->area(s)","size":9.0,"mono":true}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["struct shape  { const struct shape_ops *ops; };","struct circle { struct shape base; double r; };","// (struct shape *)&c — allowed"],"hl":[1],"lang":"c","size":8.5,"lh":20.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[19.5,31.2]}]},{"title":"Discipline","sub":"Types, NULL, lifetime","short":"Discipline","main":"Matching types, NULL checks, context lifetime.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Types must match","NULL and lifetime","Comment"],"captions":["Calling through a pointer of another type is undefined behavior, even if the code happens to work","Check an optional pointer for NULL; the context passed alongside must not die before the callback runs","A comment records: who owns the context, how long the callback lives, and where it may be called from"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["void (*f)(int) = (void (*)(int))add;","f(1);   // UB: type mismatch"],"bad":[0,1],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":22.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":28.0,"lines":["if (cb) cb(x, ctx);","","void start(void) {","    int local = 0;","    subscribe(cb, &local);   // ✕ local will die","}"],"hl":[0],"bad":[4],"lang":"c","size":9.0,"lh":17.0,"w":350.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["/* cb is called from poll();","   ctx belongs to the caller and lives","   until unsubscribe(). */"],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":20.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[13.1,34.1]}]},{"title":"A function returns a function","sub":"State machine","short":"Machine","main":"A state is a function that returns the next state.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["A function returns a function","State = function","Machine loop"],"captions":["Returning a function pointer is hard to read; typedef names the type and the syntax becomes ordinary","A state is a function that reads a char and returns the next state; C can't write a recursive type, so the pointer is wrapped in a struct","The loop calls the current state until it gets an empty one: the code reads like a transition table"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["typedef int (*binop)(int, int);","binop pick(char c);   // pick by character"],"hl":[1],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":20.0,"lines":["typedef struct state {","    struct state (*fn)(int);","} state;","state s_num(int c) {","    return isdigit(c) ? (state){s_num} : (state){s_end};","}"],"hl":[4],"lang":"c","size":8.5,"lh":16.0,"w":345.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["state s = {s_start};","for (; s.fn; s = s.fn(*p++)) {","    /* chars one at a time */","}"],"hl":[1],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":20.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[17.4,37.4]}]},{"title":"Cost of indirection","sub":"Measure","short":"Cost","main":"First correct and generic, then measure.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Direct vs indirect","Millions of calls","Rule"],"captions":["The compiler inlines a direct call into the loop; an indirect one jumps via a register, harder for the CPU to predict","A comparison called from qsort millions of times costs more than the same one baked into a loop","First write it generic and correct, then measure, and specialize only if needed"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"a","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["call cmp_int"],"lang":"asm","size":10.0,"lh":18.0,"w":110.0},{"t":"code","id":"b","x":20.0,"y":100.0,"lines":["jalr a5"],"lang":"asm","size":10.0,"lh":18.0,"w":110.0},{"t":"text","id":"t1","x":250.0,"y":40.0,"text":"address known: can inline","tone":"green","size":9.5},{"t":"text","id":"t2","x":250.0,"y":100.0,"text":"address in register: harder to predict","tone":"yellow","size":9.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a~cell","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":30.0,"text":"qsort + cmp","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b~cell","x":90.0,"y":105.0,"w":130.0,"h":30.0,"text":"own loop","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"t1","x":260.0,"y":60.0,"text":"n log n calls","size":9.5},{"t":"text","id":"t2","x":260.0,"y":105.0,"text":"cheaper","tone":"green","size":9.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a~cell","x":60.0,"y":76.0,"w":80.0,"h":30.0,"text":"correct","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b~cell","x":180.0,"y":76.0,"w":80.0,"h":30.0,"text":"measure","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":300.0,"y":76.0,"w":80.0,"h":30.0,"text":"speed up","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":100.0,"y1":76.0,"x2":140.0,"y2":76.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":220.0,"y1":76.0,"x2":260.0,"y2":76.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}]],"cues":[9.6,25.1]}]},{"title":"Strings and structs","sub":"Comparisons for qsort","short":"Comparisons","main":"For char *, a pointer to a pointer; cascade of fields.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Array of strings","Field cascade","Reverse order"],"captions":["For an array of char *, the comparison gets a pointer to a pointer: cast to char *const *, dereference, call strcmp","For structs the comparison cascades: main field first, next one on a tie; the first unequal result returns at once","Reverse order: swap the arguments; the comparison must be consistent: if a < b, then b > a"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["int by_str(const void *p, const void *q) {","    const char *a = *(char *const *)p;","    const char *b = *(char *const *)q;","    return strcmp(a, b);","}"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"c","size":8.5,"lh":18.0,"w":350.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["int c = (a->age > b->age) - (a->age < b->age);","if (c) return c;","return strcmp(a->name, b->name);"],"hl":[1],"lang":"c","size":8.5,"lh":22.0,"w":350.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["return cmp(q, p);   // descending"],"lang":"c","size":11.0,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":100.0,"text":"cmp(a, b) < 0  ⇔  cmp(b, a) > 0","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"mono":true}]],"cues":[21.4,35.0]}]},{"title":"Summary","sub":"What's next","short":"Summary","main":"Next: the preprocessor, macros, and header files.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Mechanism","Techniques","Next"],"captions":["A function pointer holds a code address and calls it indirectly, like jalr through a register","Tables replace branching, callbacks split walking from action, void * plus a size gives generic containers; qsort and bsearch are models","Watch types, context lifetime, and the cost of indirect calls; next: preprocessor, macros, and headers"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":76.0,"w":110.0,"h":34.0,"text":"code address","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":250.0,"y":76.0,"w":110.0,"h":34.0,"text":"jalr a5","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":146.0,"y1":76.0,"x2":194.0,"y2":76.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":40.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"tables","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":190.0,"y":40.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"callbacks","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":310.0,"y":40.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"void *+size","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"d","x":130.0,"y":100.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"qsort","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"e~cell","x":250.0,"y":100.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"interfaces","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":80.0,"y":76.0,"w":100.0,"h":30.0,"text":"types","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":190.0,"y":76.0,"w":100.0,"h":30.0,"text":"context","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":300.0,"y":76.0,"w":100.0,"h":30.0,"text":"cost","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":130.0,"text":"next: #define and #include","tone":"green","size":10.0,"mono":true}]],"cues":[17.4,26.8]}]}]}